# Test: a daemon that STARTS with `vpn ipsec` and no `unmatched` leaf says, at
# Error level, that the SPD catch-all DISCARD is in force by default.
# Config: vpn ipsec with one leaf, cookie-threshold, so `unmatched` takes its YANG
#         default, discard (RFC 4301 Section 4.4.1).
# Expected: the start log names the leaf, what is cut, and the two commands that
#           settle it. No commit runs at start, so refuseImplicitDiscard cannot.
#
# VALIDATES: warnImplicitDiscardAtStart (internal/component/ike/engine/unmatched.go)
#            reached through the real start: config on stdin, the ike plugin's first
#            apply (applyConfig, applyStartup).
# PREVENTS: a box booting a configuration saved before the default became discard
#           losing its own BGP and SSH with nothing in the log saying why.
#
# The noop dataplane holds the catch-all without CAP_NET_ADMIN
# (internal/component/ike/dataplane/noop.go), so the test runs unprivileged.

option=env:var=ze_test_ike_dataplane:value=noop
option=env:var=ze_test_ike_port:value=$PORT2
option=timeout:value=30s

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
vpn {
	ipsec {
		cookie-threshold 5
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=25s

await=stderr:contains=the SPD catch-all DISCARD is in force because `vpn ipsec unmatched` is not set:then=stop
expect=stderr:contains=its default is discard (RFC 4301 Section 4.4.1)
expect=stderr:contains=including this router's own BGP, SSH, DNS and NTP traffic, its ICMP
expect=stderr:contains=and its IPv6 neighbor discovery, outside a tunnel
expect=stderr:contains=the same `icmp6` entry with protocol 58 and prefix ::/0
expect=stderr:contains=`set vpn ipsec unmatched bypass` to pass that traffic
expect=stderr:contains=bypass-entries=0
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
